    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381-a1">

                <pb facs="0491" n="383" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg383"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 34.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Kurino Shinichiro
                        to Mr. Dun.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office, Tokio</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-08-01"><hi rendition="#italic">August 1,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to the intimation which I have
                    already had the honor to make to you with reference to the wreck of the merchant
                    vessel <hi rendition="#italic">North American</hi>, owned by <pb facs="0492"
                        n="384" xml:id="pg384"/> the American firm of Waitock (Reimers &amp; Co.?),
                    which was wrecked within the jurisdiction of Tokushima Ken, I now beg to inclose
                    for your information a copy of the detailed report made by the governor of
                    Tokushima Ken.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kurino Schinichiro</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Chief of the Political Bureau.<lb/>His Imperial
                            Japanese Majesty’s Department for Foreign
                    Affairs.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
